{
  "_about": "M3 noise-floor labels for the df=1 entity stratum of the 2026-07-28 snapshot.",
  "_rater": "model-labeled, single rater (Claude, 2026-07-30). FIRST PASS — contestable by design; every item ships with its raw spellings, provenance and an example headline in the companion artifact .json so a human can re-check each call.",
  "_sample": "docs/research/recall-229/2026-07-30-df1-entity-sample.json (deterministic, seed 42, keyed BY NAME)",
  "_rule": {
    "question": "Is this string a STABLE IDENTIFIER of a real entity — one an independent report of the same story would plausibly also produce? That, not grammatical entity-hood, is what makes a df=1 item usable as same-story evidence at norm_rarity 1.0.",
    "REAL": "a canonical-ish name of a real person / organisation / place / group / event / work. NER mistyping does NOT make it garbage (overlap matches on the STRING, not the type), and a SYSTEMATIC pipeline artifact that recurs identically (GDELT's leading 'a ' on person names) does not either.",
    "REAL_WEAK": "a real, stable entity that is nonetheless structurally poor same-story evidence — photo credits, reporter bylines, and the covering outlet's own name. Counted as REAL in the headline garbage rate; broken out separately because these fire on stories that share a wire desk, not a story.",
    "GARBAGE": "not a stable identifier: sentence/headline fragments, GDELT machine-translation word-salad, generic common nouns and role phrases, bare ambiguous tokens, truncations that lose the referent, two entities glued into one string, and conflations that name nobody."
  },
  "_borderline_policy": "Glued multi-entity strings ('kocaeli izmit', 'satyajit ray pather panchali') and name+modifier phrases ('trafford centre in manchester') are labeled GARBAGE even though a real name is recoverable, because a second report of the same story renders those parts separately and the glued key would never match. Honorific+name ('gen oleksandr syrskyi', 'justice shabana mahmoud') is labeled REAL because the honorific is conventional and recurs. These two calls are the main lever on the reported rate; both are stated so the number can be re-derived under a different policy.",
